        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Export a business template to its Git working copy and commit it.\n
\n
    This is the tool equivalent of the "Git" tab on a Business Template.\n
\n
    WHAT IT DOES: builds the template from the live instance, writes it into\n
    the working copy, then commits the files of that template.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - Changes made on the instance should be recorded in git.\n
    - You want to see what would be committed first (dry_run=True).\n
    - Earlier commits still have to reach the remote: call with push=True and\n
      nothing left to commit, and the pending commits are pushed on their own.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You have not reviewed what changed. Run with dry_run=True first.\n
\n
    SCOPE: every business template here shares one working copy, so the commit\n
    is restricted to the paths of the named template. Changes belonging to\n
    other templates are never included.\n
\n
    BUT belonging to the template is not the same as being yours: a shared\n
    working copy carries other people\'s in-flight work, and a template-wide\n
    commit sweeps it in under your changelog. When dry_run reports paths you\n
    did not touch, pass path_list to commit only your own -- each entry is a\n
    whole path as reported in added/modified/removed, or a prefix if it ends\n
    in \'/\' or \'*\'. What is left behind comes back in "skipped", and a\n
    path_list that matches nothing is an error rather than a silent no-op.\n
\n
    push=False by default: the commit stays local until you ask for a push.\n
    A push that does not land is reported in "warning", not as success. The\n
    "remote" block reports the remote and the upstream branch a push would go\n
    to, with any credentials in the URL redacted -- check it before pushing.\n
\n
    Returns JSON with: status (committed / pushed / dry_run / clean / error),\n
    branch, remote, revision, added, modified, removed, skipped, ahead, and\n
    pushed when a push was requested.\n
    </string> </value>
